From: oveRTOS
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/tci: call common helper signatures directly on Emscripten

TCI calls the helpers of TCG call ops through libffi. On Emscripten,
ffi_call() calls into JavaScript (ffi_call_js), which converts each
BigInt argument and calls back through the function table and
Asyncify's export wrappers. With the TB lookup off that path, a browser
profile of the vCPU thread mid shell loop and during LVGL rendering
still showed libffi at 14-16%, about two thirds of it glue. The helpers
under it were mostly the M-profile exception raisers
(exception_internal, exception_with_syndrome), then
v7m_preserve_fp_state, rebuild_hflags_m32_newel, v7m_msr, v7m_mrs and
vfp_set_fpscr.

tci.c is target-independent, so it cannot name these helpers, but they
share four signatures: (env), (env, i32) and (env, i32, i32) returning
void, and (env, i32) returning i32. On Emscripten, store each call's
typemask, from which its cif is built, after the function and cif in
the constant pool, and call these four signatures through a typed
function pointer; every other helper still goes through ffi_call().
Each argument has its own 8-byte stack slot, an i32 in the low half
that libffi reads on this little-endian host, and an i32 result goes to
stack[0], whose low half the result switch reads as after ffi_call().
Like the TB lookup, the calls run in the interpreter loop, which is
outside Asyncify, and a longjmp out of a helper unwinds only wasm
frames, as from the softmmu helpers that the interpreter calls directly.

An earlier generated switch over every helper signature (381 cases)
made rendering slower on a -O0 build whose interpreter loop Asyncify
instrumented. This one has four cases, keyed by a typemask stored once
per call site, and runs on the -O2 link with the interpreter loop
outside Asyncify. Each call's pool entry grows from 16 to 32 bytes,
and the first argument may be any pointer type, since every pointer
has the same wasm type.

On identical firmware, against 0001-0008, ffi_call() fell in profiling
builds from 19.3% to 1.9% of the vCPU thread mid shell loop and from
15.0% to 3.2% during lvbench, with exception_internal,
exception_with_syndrome and the other helpers above called directly. The
shell loop took 6.1-6.3 s, not 6.7-7.1 s, over five interleaved rounds.

---
--- a/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
+++ b/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
@@ -449,7 +449,13 @@
                          cif->rtype->size == 16);
         which = ctz32(cif->rtype->size) - 1;
     }
+#ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
+    /* tcg_qemu_tb_exec() calls some signatures directly, by typemask. */
+    new_pool_l4(s, 20, s->code_ptr, 0, (uintptr_t)func, (uintptr_t)cif,
+                info->typemask, 0);
+#else
     new_pool_l2(s, 20, s->code_ptr, 0, (uintptr_t)func, (uintptr_t)cif);
+#endif
     insn = deposit32(insn, 0, 8, INDEX_op_call);
     insn = deposit32(insn, 8, 4, which);
     tcg_out32(s, insn);
--- a/tcg/tci.c
+++ b/tcg/tci.c
@@ -390,6 +390,37 @@
     }
 }
 
+#ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
+/*
+ * libffi calls through JavaScript on Emscripten.  Call helpers of the
+ * signatures common on M-profile directly, keyed by the typemask that
+ * tcg_out_call() stores after the cif, and leave any result where
+ * ffi_call() does.  An i32 argument is the low half of its slot.
+ */
+static inline bool QEMU_DISABLE_CFI tci_call_direct(void *func,
+                                                    tcg_target_ulong typemask,
+                                                    uint64_t *stack)
+{
+    void *a0 = (void *)(uintptr_t)stack[0];
+
+    switch (typemask) {
+    case dh_typemask(ptr, 1):
+        ((void (*)(void *))func)(a0);
+        return true;
+    case dh_typemask(ptr, 1) | dh_typemask(i32, 2):
+        ((void (*)(void *, uint32_t))func)(a0, stack[1]);
+        return true;
+    case dh_typemask(ptr, 1) | dh_typemask(i32, 2) | dh_typemask(i32, 3):
+        ((void (*)(void *, uint32_t, uint32_t))func)(a0, stack[1], stack[2]);
+        return true;
+    case dh_typemask(i32, 0) | dh_typemask(ptr, 1) | dh_typemask(i32, 2):
+        stack[0] = ((uint32_t (*)(void *, uint32_t))func)(a0, stack[1]);
+        return true;
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+#endif
+
 /* Interpret pseudo code in tb. */
 /*
  * Disable CFI checks.
@@ -454,7 +485,8 @@
                 if (func == (void *)helper_lookup_tb_ptr) {
                     stack[0] = (uintptr_t)helper_lookup_tb_ptr(
                         (CPUArchState *)(uintptr_t)stack[0]);
-                } else {
+                } else if (!tci_call_direct(func, ((tcg_target_ulong *)ptr)[2],
+                                            stack)) {
                     ffi_call(cif, func, stack, call_slots);
                 }
 #else
